    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> army of some 20,000 armed mainly with spears and cowhide shields overran about 1,300 British and colonial troops with modern rifles, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederic-thesiger-2nd-baron-chelmsford">Lord Chelmsford</a> had divided his force and left the camp unentrenched.</li><li>Estimates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> dead run from 1,000 to 3,000, since neither the British nor the Zulu counted them; of the British force, over 1,300 were killed.</li><li>The defeat made the British government commit to a heavily reinforced second invasion and ended King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetshwayo">Cetshwayo</a>'s hopes of a negotiated peace.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A solar eclipse fell at 2:30 pm on the day of the battle, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> warrior recalled that the sun turned black in the middle of the fighting and then came out bright again.</p></aside>
    </section>

